From: isoriano1968 <isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] dtlogin: register the user with AMIX's user licensing

AMIX's kernel kills a non-root process with a controlling terminal at its
first fork unless it descends from a registered login; login(1) and our
sshd register with sysm68k(_m68k_LIMUSER, EUA_ADD_USER).  dtlogin did not,
so in a CDE session the shell in every dtterm died at its first command.
Register in the session child while still root, before setuid().
---
--- a/programs/dtlogin/session.c	2026-11-03 13:23:02.766932130 +0100
+++ b/programs/dtlogin/session.c	2026-11-03 13:23:02.778932165 +0100
@@ -73,6 +73,12 @@
 #endif
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <pwd.h>
+#ifdef __amix__
+/* from <sys/sysm68k.h>, which hides them unless m68k is defined (gcc 14 has __m68k__) */
+#define _m68k_LIMUSER	95
+#define EUA_ADD_USER	4
+int sysm68k(int, ...);
+#endif
 #include <dirent.h>
 #include <limits.h>
 
@@ -1514,6 +1520,18 @@
 	setaudproc(verify->audflg);
 #  endif
 
+#ifdef __amix__
+	/*
+	 * AMIX's user licensing: a non-root process with a controlling
+	 * terminal (the shell in a dtterm) is killed at its first fork
+	 * unless it descends from a registered login, as login(1)
+	 * registers itself.  Only root may register: do it here, before
+	 * setuid(), so the session and everything it starts inherit it.
+	 */
+	if (sysm68k(_m68k_LIMUSER, EUA_ADD_USER) == -1)
+	    Debug("sysm68k EUA_ADD_USER failed, errno = %d\n", errno);
+#endif
+
 /* setpenv() will set uid for AIX */
 #if !defined(_AIX)
 	if (setuid(verify->uid) != 0) {
